    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d759">

                <pb facs="1033" n="1019" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg1019"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.932/21: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-16T10:00:00+07:00">May 16, 1944—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 16—7:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>857. Political Vice-Foreign Minister last evening volunteered to Counselor
                    information that Chinese draft treaty would be completed not later than month
                    hence (re our 777, May 4<anchor n="22" xml:id="d759-f1"/>). When asked if draft
                    would also be presented to British, Vice-Minister said that was another
                    question, but we could be assured that we would be “among the first” to receive
                    it.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
